# Public keys authorised for $(USER_LOGIN) on every built image.
#
# Baked in on purpose: the rootfs cutover replaces the whole filesystem, so
# a key added by hand to a running device survives only until its next OTA.
# See SSH_AUTHORIZED_KEYS in the Makefile.
#
# This is also flash-nmap.sh's PRIMARY ownership gate — criterion 1 is that
# BatchMode key auth succeeds and 'sudo -n' grants root. A device that does
# not accept one of these is not recognised as ours and is skipped, so an
# image built without this file makes a whole fleet invisible to a sweep.
#
# A DEDICATED fleet key, deliberately not a personal identity: units get
# handed to a contractor, and the key that can root the fleet should be
# rotatable without touching anyone's own ~/.ssh. Private half lives at
# ~/.ssh/junkyard-fleet on the build host and is NOT in this repo.
# Use it with: flash-nmap.sh -i ~/.ssh/junkyard-fleet   (adds IdentitiesOnly)
#              flash-ssh.sh  SSH_OPTS='-i ~/.ssh/junkyard-fleet'
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIK7Vvm4sWJOH7kuwRjw9VKVDvnWKlfNdUkBdOmrmCyPO junkyard-fleet deploy key
